      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, some European countries with wealth taxes, such as France, have indeed seen a significant \"flight to quality\" effect, where wealthy individuals relocate their assets to jurisdictions with lower tax burdens, such as Switzerland or the Cayman Islands. This can be a major issue for governments, as it undermines the tax base and can reduce revenue. This phenomenon has raised concerns among policymakers that a wealth tax could be difficult to implement effectively, as wealthy individuals may seek to avoid it by reconfiguring their wealth structures or relocating abroad.",
      "source": "target",
